SOURCE CODE ASSOCIATION

Every distributed binary must be accompanied by a release manifest that
identifies the release version, Android versionCode, application ID, exact
source commit, recipient-accessible corresponding-source location, and
SHA-256 digests for the APK, AAB, and source archive. Generate that manifest
after all artifacts exist and distribute it beside the binary and source
archive.

Do not embed an artifact's own digest in that artifact. A private Git
repository that release recipients cannot access is not a
recipient-accessible corresponding-source location. The release record must
either provide corresponding source through the same distribution channel or
use another GPL-compliant source-delivery method.

